# Line endings are pinned here, not left to each machine's git setting.
#
# Why: sentinel_run.cmd is a batch file. A batch file with Unix line endings and a
# multi-line parenthesised block is parsed wrongly -- the statements after the block
# are skipped and the exit code is still 0. The launcher therefore ships with Windows
# line endings and one statement per line; this file makes a clone or a ZIP download
# deliver exactly that, whatever the reader's git configuration says.

* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.vbs text eol=crlf

# A screenshot of the toast goes in docs/. Git detects binary files by itself; this line
# only makes the intent explicit, so text conversion can never touch it.
*.png binary
